## The RPN Calculator

This section needs the optional forth.py file next to wypyplus.py. Without it, RPN(...) and table formulas are shown as plain text.

The built-in RPN calculator supports 
* Basic math operations: +, -, *, /, and ^(pow)
* Control flow: if else then
* Compare: > < =
* Stack operations: dup, over, swap, drop, and rot
* Other functions: sqrt, abs, log, sin, cos, tan, and int
* Print operations: .

### Basic Math
{|
| 1 1 + || RPN(1 1 +) 
|-
| 1 1 - || RPN(1 1 -)
|-
| 2 2 * || RPN(2 2 *)
|-
| 10 5 / || RPN(10 5 /)
|-
| 2 3 ^ || RPN(2 3 ^)
|-
| Print error message: || RPN(2 3 abcde)
|} 

### Control Flow
{|
| 2 3 > if "yes" else "no" then || RPN(2 3 > if "yes" else "no" then) 
|-
| "a" "a" = if "yes" else "no" then || RPN("a" "a" = if "yes" else "no" then)
|}

### User Defined Functions
A user can define new functions with the following syntax:

RPN (: <fun name> <fun content> ;)

Two examples:

RPN (: squire dup * ;)
RPN(: squire dup * ;)

RPN (: pythagoras squire swap squire + sqrt ;)
RPN(: pythagoras squire swap squire + sqrt ;)



